<title>USA: Western Resources sees cash flow accretion.</title>
<headline>Western Resources sees cash flow accretion.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Resources chairman John Hayes said the company's proposed $3.5 billion acquisition of ADT Ltd would be &quot;significantly&quot; cash flow accretive in the first year of the transaction.</p>
<p>He also told reporters in a conference call that the proposed transaction would be accretive to earnings &quot;in a few years.&quot;</p>
<p>He did not elaborate.</p>
<p>((--Robin Sidel, 212/859-1723))</p>
</text>
